The page links one other kill chain and five defense topics.

It says this chain's shape matches Polyfill.io in 2024, where the domain behind a widely embedded script was sold and its new owner served malicious code to every site still loading it. Here, DebugBear has not described any change of ownership.

The page's related defense topics are API and web security, how CSOH.org is secured, CI/CD and supply chain, incident response, and detection engineering. CI/CD stands for continuous integration and continuous delivery.
